    {
      "id": "game-description-ccc1bdfd-5ffe-44d9-bf26-f989dc3b942f-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Mixed martial arts combines striking and grappling within one combat sport. Competitors move between distance fighting, clinches, takedowns, and ground positions, so success depends on connecting skills that other disciplines may practice separately. Bouts can be decided by a finish or by judges under the rules of the event."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-ccc1bdfd-5ffe-44d9-bf26-f989dc3b942f-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Modern MMA developed through cross-style competition and several regional traditions, including Brazilian vale tudo. It should not be reduced to the invention of one promoter or organization. Different organizations and historical periods have used different rules, even as regulated competition has developed shared conventions."
    },
